# Computability

The modern spelling of the mark@index[Turing, Alan] and of a
subentry@index[computability!decidability], plus a sorted display form
whose entry contains brackets@index[alpha@$f[x]$] — the raw balanced
scan has to survive the generic `@name[…]` directive tokenizer.

A named index@index[Church, Alonzo]{name=authors} still works, and the
legacy spelling:index[legacy mark] is still accepted.

## Disambiguation

Marks are glued to the word they index, which is why this is the one `@`
form that may follow a word character directly.

A bare `@index` is the placement, not a mark: only the bracket tells them
apart. Both forms are shown literally here — `@index[entry]` and
`@index{title="…"}` — inside code spans, so neither is claimed.

@index{title="Subject Index" intoc}

@index{name=authors title="Author Index"}
